The OpenCode-Go API key used by the probe scripts is **not** stored in this
repository: it is read from the `OPENCODE_GO_KEY` environment variable, and the
WorkBuddy gateway key from `WB_GATEWAY_KEY`. Where each credential comes from
is documented in docs/SECRETS.md (locations only, never values).

==============================================================================
Third-party services and components
==============================================================================

This project drives, but does NOT redistribute, the following third-party
software and services. No third-party source code is included in this
repository.

- WorkBuddy2API Panel (a multi-account gateway for Tencent CodeBuddy)
  https://github.com/linguo2625469/workbuddy2api-panel
  Original project: https://github.com/Sliverkiss/workbuddy2api
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Why used: it exposes a Tencent CodeBuddy account pool as an
  OpenAI-compatible HTTP endpoint on 127.0.0.1:7863, which lets the
  WorkBuddy models be used from the ZCode client. This repository only
  sends HTTP requests to it; the gateway binary and its source are NOT
  distributed with this repository. A local working clone may live at
  workbuddy/gateway/ (with its own .git), but that directory is git-ignored
  and is not part of the published tree. The MIT license text of the
  upstream project is reproduced below for reference.

- OpenCode Zen / Go (opencode.ai)
  https://opencode.ai/
  A commercial, subscription-based model service. Not open source; it is
  governed by the OpenCode terms of service, not by an open-source license.
  Why used: it provides the "Go" model plan and the
  https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1 API endpoint that this repository probes and
  syncs into the ZCode client. No OpenCode code is included here.

- ZCode (the target client) — **Apache-2.0**, open-sourced by Zhipu on 2026-09-21
  https://github.com/zai-org/ZCode
  Why used: it is the client whose model list this repository populates. This
  repository reads and writes the user's own configuration file
  (~/.zcode/v2/provider_config.json) and reproduces the client's request-body
  semantics by replaying the engine's own rule resolution.
  **Files distributed in this repository** (see third-party/zcode/UPSTREAM.md
  for the pinned commit):
    - config/provider/zcode-builtin.json  — the built-in rule data
    - packages/provider/src/config/model-config.ts — ModelConfigRules.resolve()
    - packages/provider/src/config/schema.ts — rule flattening order
    - packages/provider/src/config/rule-data-schema.ts — rule schema
  These are unmodified upstream files, redistributed under Apache-2.0; the
  Apache-2.0 license text is reproduced in third-party/zcode/LICENSE.

- Python 3 (Python Software Foundation)
  https://www.python.org/
  Licensed under the Python Software Foundation License.
  Why used: runtime for the .py scripts (standard library only).

- Node.js (OpenJS Foundation)
  https://nodejs.org/
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Why used: runtime for the .js scripts (header-injection proxy, effective-body
  resolver, thinking-off probe).

- MetaCubeX / mihomo / ShellCrash
  NOT used by this repository. Those components belong to the router /
  proxy line of the original working directory and were not carried over
  into this split. No MetaCubeX code or data is present here.

